This Collection Consists of A Group of Black and White Photography (from the Late 19th Century) Showing Black People in A Variety of Activities Such As Playing Cricket, Dancing, Singing, Attending A Slave Action, Standing at Railroad Station in Louisiana, Meeting Frriends at Ball, Dancing Under the Stars in a New Orleans Severayard, Dancing in Front of a Bonfire, Gathering Herbs for Making Medicinal Folk Remedies, Attending Church on Sunday Mornings, Listening to Female Solo Soprano at Union Square In New York City; serving as well as doing farm work; Attending to Funeral; Walking Down the Aisle During the Wedding Ceremony; Visiting Friends; Participating in Community Celebrations Such as Mardi Gras; and playing games. Notably Excluded are photography of Black Entertainers Such the Minstrel Shows.

